      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can mix dextromethorphan with sertraline without a major issue, but be careful with other sedatives since both can make you drowsy.\nI recommend taking a cough syrup with dextromethorphan at night, but avoid any products containing codeine or strong antihistamines like diphenhydramine.\nIf your cough persists beyond a week or you develop a fever, you should see a doctor immediately.",
